  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Union (EU) Support to Ukrainian Integrated Border Management (IBM) Actors in the Context of the Ongoing War in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 24 February 2022, the full-scale invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation has contributed to increased security threats, including in the Transnistria region of the Republic of Moldova which borders Ukraine. This project seeks to contributing to Ukraine&#x2019;s trade facilitation and economic recovery through improving flows of essential goods through Border Crossing Points (BCPs) and supporting the enhanced resilience and business continuity of Ukrainian border and migration authorities in the context of the ongoing Russian full-scale war against Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
